Vendored from zimg, unmodified except that "common/x.h" includes are flattened to "x.h".

Source revision: release-3.0.6-251-g274b46e

Why these files are copied rather than used from libzimg: zimg installs only
src/zimg/api/zimg.h and zimg++.hpp, and links with -export-symbols-regex '^zimg_',
so the colorspace matrix helpers are neither declared nor exported in a system build.
VapourSynth resolves zimg through dependency('zimg') with the subproject only as a
fallback, so on any distro build these symbols do not exist.

What is used: the colorspace helpers turn primaries and matrix enums into 3x3 matrices
for the GPU resize's fused colour kernel -- pure scalar math with no SIMD and no
dependency on zimg's execution engine. The resampling side of the GPU path evaluates
its kernels in the shader and needs nothing from here.

Keeping this in step with the zimg the CPU path links against is manual. If the two
drift, the GPU path's colour constants stop matching resize's, which is exactly the
difference the differential tests are meant to catch -- so re-copy on a zimg bump.
